{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Eviction Law good-cause grounds and notice","requirement":"A landlord may evict a residential tenant only for the good causes listed in the Eviction Law, such as nonpayment of rent, disorderly conduct, or specified criminal convictions; a three-day Notice to Quit is required for the criminal-activity grounds.","key_value":"3-day Notice to Quit","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental dwellings; tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings may be removed only by court order and only for a limited list of causes.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings have a limited cause list and three-month or one-month notice."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the tenant's damages plus attorney fees and costs for misuse of an owner-occupancy or demolition eviction; a civil penalty up to $10,000 for each violation of the five-year residential-use ban.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No eviction suit may be brought more than two years after: the juvenile was found to be delinquent; conviction of the person; or after the person’s release from incarceration, whichever is later. A Notice to Quit must be served on the tenant at least three day s prior to filing a suit for (N.J.S.A. 2A-18-61.1(o)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey tenant anti-reprisal protection","requirement":"A landlord may not retaliate against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of the lease or its terms, or refusal to renew when the tenant exercises specified civil rights, such as enforcing lease or law rights or organizing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes; owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings are excepted.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excepts owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings."},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","penalty":"The tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act","requirement":"A landlord converting a building to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership may not evict eligible senior or disabled tenants who lived there at least one year before the conversion; eligible tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years.","key_value":"40 years","coverage_conditions":"Tenants at least 62 before the conversion recording date, permanently disabled, or certain disabled veterans, residing in the building at least one year before conversion; income-limited.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Buildings being converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.22","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county or $50,000.00, whichever  is greater (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992","requirement":"The 1992 amendment extends protected tenancy to qualified tenants in qualified counties, in buildings converted or being converted, who were not eligible under the Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act; Hudson County is the only qualified county.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Qualified tenants in qualified counties (currently only Hudson County) in buildings converted or being converted, not eligible under the 1981 senior/disabled protected tenancy law.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Only Hudson County qualifies."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"The Tenant Protection Law of 1992 amendment extends protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible for Protected Tenancy as either Senior Citizens or Disabled Persons under the “Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act of 1981” (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40 to -61.59; N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.1 to -3.4).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on rent increases above rent control or unreasonable increases","requirement":"A landlord may not raise rent above any applicable rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or, where the property is not rent controlled, may not impose an unreasonable or unconscionable rent increase.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwellings subject to a rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or not rent controlled.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":null,"quoted_span":"An increase in rent in excess of any rent control or rent leveling ordinance, or if the property is not subject to rent control, an unreasonable or unconscionable rent increase.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.5,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
